4139538894 17592186045443 true] [17592186674089 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4y &=-2 \\\\ 4x-7y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139538894 17592186045443 true] [17592186674089 1072 #uuid "22f5a49d-093c-5c2d-bc11-d9f90e179350" 13194139538894 17592186045443 true] [17592186674089 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-1 \\\\ y &=1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(1)=-1\\,⇒\\,x=1.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=1$ and $y=1.$" 13194139538894 17592186045443 true] [17592186674090 1080 "$$\nM∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right],\n$$\n$\\,x=-4$ and $y=-2$" 13194139538894 17592186045443 true] [17592186674090 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538894 17592186045443 true] [17592186674090 1083 #uuid "289e2ffe-8f18-537c-a0e0-2c55bbd9348f" 13194139538894 17592186045443 true] [17592186674091 1080 "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{array}\\right]" 13194139538894 17592186045443 true] [17592186674091 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538894 17592186045443 true] [17592186674091 1083 #uuid "2cedabad-e0ff-5c7e-